/-!
# Smoothing a global complete intersection over a field

A global complete intersection `A` over a field `k` is the special fibre of a flat finite type
`k⟦X⟧`-algebra whose generic fibre, over the field of formal Laurent series `k⸨X⸩`, is smooth.
Specializing each deformation parameter of the universal affine-linear deformation to a power
series in `(X)` that avoids the hypersurface cut out by generic smoothness leaves the special
fibre equal to `A` and makes the generic fibre smooth. Localizing at an element congruent to `1`
modulo `X` does not change the special fibre, and shrinks the family to the locus where the
fibre-dimension criterion for relative complete intersections applies, which gives flatness and
finite type.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.Smoothing.exists_flat_powerSeries_specialFiber_smooth_genericFiber`:
  a global complete intersection over `k` is the special fibre of a flat finite type
  `k⟦X⟧`-algebra with smooth generic fibre.

## Implementation notes

The special fibre of a `k⟦X⟧`-algebra `B` is the quotient of `B` by the ideal generated by the
image of `X`, which is the source's `B/tB`. The generic fibre is the base change
`k⸨X⸩ ⊗[k⟦X⟧] B`; the canonical map `k⟦X⟧ → k⸨X⸩` inverts `X`, so this is the source's
`B[1/t]`. The scalar-tower hypotheses record that the `k`-algebra structure on `B` is the one
induced by its `k⟦X⟧`-algebra structure.

The dimension equality in the main result is conditional on `Nontrivial A`, because a global
complete intersection is also allowed to be the zero ring, whose Krull dimension is `⊥`. The
base field and the algebra being smoothed have independent universes; the witness lies in the
universe of the field, as does the source's quotient of a polynomial ring in finitely many
variables over `k⟦X⟧`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7V)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
